In terms of size and proportions, tomatoes vary widely depending on the variety. The ones shown here appear to be medium-sized, typical of cherry or plum tomatoes. Their size is consistent across all three images.

There are no specific behavioral characteristics unique to tomatoes as they are plants and do not exhibit behaviors like animals do. However, their growth process involves photosynthesis and requires sunlight, water, and nutrients.

Unique identifying traits include their round shape, smooth texture, and vibrant color. The presence of stems and leaves in some images further distinguishes them from other fruits or vegetables.
